      "id": 1,
      "text": "Delmita was founded in 1919 as Zaragosa by Peña, Sr., before changing its name in 1931 to avoid mail confusion with Saragosa.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        5,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/delmita-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Delmita’s first post office opened shortly after the town’s founding, and a new building was erected in 1991.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delmita%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early mail delivery to Delmita was carried by horseback three times a week, with riders exchanging horses in Zaragosa before heading to Rio Grande City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/delmita-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community lies on a paved county road halfway between the old site of El Centro on Farm Road 2294 and La Reforma on Farm Road 1017.",
